# Entes MPR-63.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | ENTES MPR-63 3-Phase Power Analyzer (Modbus RTU RS-485)
# | 
# | Source: entes-mpr-63-series-kullanma-talimati-tr.pdf (Turkish manual, Chapter 3)
# | Protocol: Modbus RTU; FC03 read, FC06 single-register write, FC10 multi-register write
# | Function codes: 03H=read, 06H=write single, 10H=write multiple, 14H=data record read, 2BH=device info
# | Modbus slave address: set via DIP switch on device (1-247)
# | All addresses are 0-based decimal = hex address from manual.
# | 
# | Scale factors for 16-bit table (section 3.12):
# | Voltage LN/LL: raw × VT × 0.1 = V (VT = voltage transformer ratio, read from addr 75)
# | Current:       raw × CT × 0.001 = A (CT = current transformer ratio, read from addr 74)
# | Active power:  raw × VT × CT = W (signed)
# | Reactive power:raw × VT × CT = VAr (signed)
# | Apparent power:raw × VT × CT = VA (unsigned)
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Entes
@model=MPR-63
@vendor_website=entes.com.tr
@description=3-phase power analyzer, Modbus RTU. 16-bit measurement table at addr 0-84 (FC03): LN/LL voltages (×VT×0.1 V), currents (×CT×0.001 A), per-phase+total active/reactive/apparent power, PF+cos-phi (×0.001), frequency (×0.01 Hz), THD per phase (×0.1 %), min/max voltages, demand currents+powers, energy import/export (MSB/LSB word pair). I/O relay status/control at addr 76 (bit0=Relay1, bit1=Relay2; MPR63-10/20/40 also bit2=Input1, bit3=Input2). Settings at 256-364 (FC03/06): CT/VT ratio, connection type, relay 1-2 thresholds, log intervals, demand time, RTC set, serial number. 32-bit table at 0x4000 (addr 16384, ×0.01). Harmonics at 0x0200/0x0300.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/entes-mpr-63.toml; Source: entes-mpr-63-series-kullanma-talimati-tr.pdf (Turkish manual, Chapter 3). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

